1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,755
Every morning in my grandmother's
house began the same way: with smoke,

2
00:00:08,755 --> 00:00:11,138
and with coffee.

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:19,915
She roasted the green beans over the
fire until they cracked and turned dark,

4
00:00:19,915 --> 00:00:24,069
and the whole house smelled of it.

5
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:33,039
Then she carried the smoking pan to
each of us. Breathe it in, she said.

6
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:37,186
This is how a day should start.

7
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:46,420
The first cup is called abol. It is
the strongest. It is for waking up.

8
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,402
The second cup, tona, was for talking.

9
00:00:49,402 --> 00:00:52,906
This is where all the
family stories came out.

10
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:59,852
The third cup is baraka, the blessing.
Nobody leaves before the third cup,

11
00:00:59,852 --> 00:01:01,619
she always told us.

12
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:08,954
Now our family lives in four
cities and two countries.

13
00:01:08,954 --> 00:01:13,700
We rarely sit together for three cups.

14
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:20,595
But when I make coffee, I
still roast it the slow way.

15
00:01:20,595 --> 00:01:25,359
And I always wait for the third cup.
